Hi Logan,
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I wanted to document a couple of utility issues in H Loop=
 and my attempts to clarify the protocol for handling guest concerns.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Yesterday afternoon, the water was temporarily turned off=
. During that time, three guests came to my site to ask about the outage, o=
ne of whom was particularly aggressive. I mentioned this to Kati when she p=
assed by.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">This morning at 3 AM, the power went out in H Loop. Antic=
ipating that guests might come to me with questions, I reached out to Kati =
at 6 AM for guidance on protocol and whether I should contact someone for u=
pdates in future outages.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Here=92s the exchange for documentation:</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Me:</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">&quot;Hi, Kati. This is Sam, in H Loop across from the ga=
te. H Loop lost power at 3am. I understand this happens but after yesterday=
, I now know I own this problem in the eyes of guests. I wanted to reach ou=
t to discover the protocol for these kinds
 of situations. Do I call you, regardless of the hour? Can I get an update =
in case someone asks me about it? Thanks and hope you're well.&quot;</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Kati:</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">&quot;You definitely don't own the problem, it's likely a=
n issue with our power company, Central Lincoln. They're usually very quick=
 at restoring power depending on how many other outages there are and staff=
ing. If people come to you just let them
 know it will be restored as soon as possible. Do you know if the entire lo=
op lost power?&quot;</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I responded to let her know it appeared to be the whole l=
oop and that my goal was simply to have the information I needed when guest=
s approached me. The power was restored around 6:45 AM.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I=92m not requesting any action, just documenting what ha=
ppened. Let me know if there=92s anything I should be doing differently in =
these situations.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Thanks,</div>
Sam
<div dir=3D"auto"></div>
<div dir=3D"auto"></div>
